description: Authentication identity comes only from a validated principal
globs: src/Backend/**/*.cs
alwaysApply: false
---

# Authentication & identity

- The authenticated `UserId` is taken only from `ICurrentUser`, which is
  populated from a cryptographically validated principal (JWT Bearer:
  signature, issuer, audience, lifetime). Never from body, query, route,
  or unvalidated headers.
- `ITenantRlsSessionFactory.OpenAsync` must not accept a caller-supplied
  `userId`. Tenant id is a selection hint and still requires an Active
  Membership.
- Do not put tenant roles in JWT claims. Membership is database-backed.
- Passwords are hashed with ASP.NET Core `PasswordHasher<User>`. Never
  store or log plaintext passwords.
- PostgreSQL `app.current_user_id` and `app.current_tenant_id` must be
  SET LOCAL (transaction-scoped) so pooled connections cannot leak
  identity. Set `current_user_id` before membership lookup; set
  `current_tenant_id` only after membership succeeds.
- `memberships` RLS is `user_id = current_user_id`, not tenant id, so
  bootstrap is not circular.
- Platform administration stays out of User and Membership.
